ding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB) / Therapy-Related AML:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB) / Therapy-Related AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology"}
